# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
# The dashboard is a client-side-routed SPA (see src/lib/routes.ts): /review,
# /graph, /flow, etc. are rendered in the browser, not as separate HTML files.
# Without this rule a hard load of a deep link (or a refresh on /review) 404s.
# Mirror of the Netlify `[[redirects]] /* -> /index.html 200` in netlify.toml.
#
# A genuinely-missing hashed asset must 404 — NOT fall through to the SPA
# catch-all below, which would hand back text/html (the index) for a .js/.css
# request and trip a MIME/parse error on a stale client. Real assets are served
# by Cloudflare before _redirects fire, so this only catches missing ones.
/assets/*  /404.html  404
/*  /index.html  200
